diagnosis_text:
Affected component: FRR BGP ECMP configuration on the leaf routers. Mechanism: Each leaf learns two equal-cost eBGP paths to the opposite rack’s subnet via both spines, but only a single “best” path is being installed in the RIB due to standard BGP tie-break (lowest router-id), so all east–west traffic funnels through one spine. Evidence: On leaf_router_0_0, “show ip bgp 10.0.1.0/24” shows two paths via 172.16.0.4 (AS 65100) and 172.16.0.8 (AS 65101), but “show ip route 10.0.1.0/24” installs only 172.16.0.4. On leaf_router_0_1, “show ip bgp 10.0.0.0/24” shows two paths via 172.16.0.6 and 172.16.0.10, yet “show ip route 10.0.0.0/24” installs only 172.16.0.6. Both leaf FRR configs lack multipa
